        <value>Logs exclude filenames, paths, photos, thumbnails, Exif/XMP/IPTC metadata, GPS coordinates, arbitrary native exception messages, network endpoints and stable device identifiers. Windows crash reports are separate.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyRetention.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Logs are limited by size and file count, without a fixed number of days: at most 256 KiB in total, 64 retained record files and 4,096 bytes per record.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyExportHeading.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>What if I share a log?</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyExport.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Export local diagnostics opens a Windows file picker so you can choose where to save a size-limited, revalidated snapshot of sanitized records. It does not export arbitrary files from the log folder. Nothing is sent automatically.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyExternalHeading.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>What about cloud folders and websites?</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyContactHeading.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Questions? Get in touch</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyContact.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Hadden Industries cannot retrieve files kept only on your device. If you email us or choose to share an export, your correspondence and anything you include are handled under the publisher's separate privacy policy. Share journals, photos or personal details only if you intend to do so.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_SettingsIntroHeading.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Set up your next spin</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyQuickLocal.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Photos are processed on this device</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyQuickUpload.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>No app upload service</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyQuickShare.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Share logs only when you choose</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyCloudSummary.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Cloud folders can still sync through their provider. Windows and Microsoft Store may collect diagnostics under their own settings and policies.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyProcessingSafety.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Analyzing photos does not alter them. After you review the proposed work, the app creates corrected copies or replaces originals according to your Output choice. Replacement can retain a verified backup or proceed without one; without a backup, the app cannot restore the original bytes. Hadden Industries receives neither photos nor metadata from the app.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyOperationalData.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Photos, corrected copies, verified backups and recovery journals are separate from diagnostic logs. The diagnostic cleanup limit does not apply to them. Backups do not expire automatically.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyRecoverySafety.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Keep backups and recovery data until interrupted work is reconciled and you no longer need recovery. Deleting them can prevent recovery. Resetting or uninstalling the app does not delete copies or exports in other folders.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyDiagnosticsFormat.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Logs use UTF-8 JSON Lines (.jsonl) files in the app-local LocalDiagnostics folder.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyStorageDetails.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>A reserved pending record counts toward the storage budget and is never exported. The empty writer-lease file is not a record. Cleanup removes only recognized, validated diagnostic records.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyUnknownFiles.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Unknown, corrupt or unsupported files are left alone. If the app cannot validate a file, logging or export stops instead of deleting or sharing it. Photo processing can continue even when logging fails.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyExportChoices.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Review the export before sharing it: times, outcomes and resource limits may still be sensitive. You decide who receives it and when to delete it.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyExportPartial.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>An error or cancellation may leave a partial file at the destination. Export is not guaranteed to be atomic.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Shell_PrivacyWindowsServices.Text" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Windows and Microsoft Store can handle crash reporting, installation information and other diagnostics under their policies and your Windows choices. Those services are separate from the app's local logs.</value>
    </data>
